# Adopt first (Pulse Perch)

Before writing new desk logic, **find the thing people already trust** and wrap it. Modular files still don’t excuse inventing a second wallet stack.

## Gate (chat, before tools)
1. **Need:** one sentence.
2. **Adopt:** named lib / API / sibling repo (or “none exists because…”).
3. **Glue:** what thin file we add under `src/ui|chain|wc|trezor/`.
4. **Not inventing:** the engine we refuse to rewrite.

Map: [OPEN-SOURCE-INFRA.md](../../OPEN-SOURCE-INFRA.md).

## Already decided — don’t re-litigate
| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Chain I/O | **viem** |
| Device | **`@trezor/connect-web`** → Suite |
| Sites | **Reown WalletKit** |
| QR | **qrcode** |
| Shell | **Vite + React** |
| History | **PulseScan / Blockscout HTTP** |
| Swap route | **PulseX** router — wrap, don’t AMM |
| Fiat | **ProveX** deep link — don’t custody |

## Forbidden
- Homegrown RPC client, WC stack, Connect substitute, indexer, AMM, fiat ramp
- “Quick custom X” when npm already has a maintained X (focus trap, QR, multicall helpers, ABI tools)

## Allowed invent
Pulse-first chrome, Suite-gap copy, clear-sign strips, dead-end recipient guards, Trezor confirm UX — the product face, not the rails.
